WEBVTT

1
00:01:46.541 --> 00:01:49.166
Arjun, now able through the divine sight

2
00:01:49.166 --> 00:01:53.291
given by Lord Krishna to behold the Vishwarupa,

3
00:01:53.291 --> 00:01:56.333
begins to describe all

4
00:01:56.333 --> 00:01:58.583
that he sees.

5
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:01.375
He sees the entire universe

6
00:02:01.375 --> 00:02:03.416
within Lord Krishna's body,

7
00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:04.916
from the highest planets

8
00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:07.583
where Brahma resides,

9
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:09.875
to the lowest realms,

10
00:02:09.875 --> 00:02:13.791
where divine serpents like Vasuki dwell.

11
00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:16.041
This vision confirms

12
00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:20.375
that everything is contained
within Lord Krishna.

13
00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:26.041
Arjun,

14
00:02:26.041 --> 00:02:29.208
still seated on his chariot,

15
00:02:29.208 --> 00:02:30.416
begins to describe

16
00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:34.166
the wondrous, awe-inspiring form

17
00:02:34.166 --> 00:02:35.791
before him.

18
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:36.750
He sees all

19
00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.041
the heavenly beings –

20
00:02:38.041 --> 00:02:40.500
the devas, the rishis, and the mighty

21
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.458
cosmic forces –

22
00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:46.250
all present within Lord Krishna's body.

23
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.625
He specifically mentions
Brahma seated on the lotus,

24
00:02:49.625 --> 00:02:52.791
the great rishis, and divine

25
00:02:52.791 --> 00:02:56.625
serpents like Vasuki and Ananta.

26
00:02:56.625 --> 00:03:00.083
This means that from the
highest point of creation

27
00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:01.125
to the lowest realms,

28
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:05.000
everything is within Lord Krishna.

29
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.041
As Arjun looks on,

30
00:03:07.041 --> 00:03:10.166
he grasps the vastness of this form.

31
00:03:10.166 --> 00:03:13.250
He sees countless arms, stomachs,

32
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.416
faces, and eyes,

33
00:03:15.416 --> 00:03:17.833
stretching in all directions.

34
00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:21.541
This form is infinite in size and presence.

35
00:03:21.541 --> 00:03:25.583
There is no clear beginning, middle, or end.

36
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:28.041
Lord Krishna, who is Vishveshvara,

37
00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:31.250
the master of the universe, is now showing

38
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:33.291
that His power and presence

39
00:03:33.291 --> 00:03:36.750
extend beyond all limits.

40
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.208
The intensity of this vision is overwhelming.

41
00:03:40.208 --> 00:03:44.125
This is not just a large or powerful form.

42
00:03:44.125 --> 00:03:46.041
It is a form

43
00:03:46.041 --> 00:03:49.083
radiating immense divine light.

44
00:03:49.083 --> 00:03:52.458
Arjun describes it as aprameyam,

45
00:03:52.458 --> 00:03:55.958
that which cannot be measured.

46
00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:56.833
He compares it

47
00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:58.166
to blazing fire

48
00:03:58.166 --> 00:04:00.000
or the blinding brilliance

49
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.750
of the sun.

50
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.625
This means its radiance

51
00:04:03.625 --> 00:04:05.916
is beyond human comprehension.

52
00:04:05.916 --> 00:04:08.541
Even though Arjun has divine sight,

53
00:04:08.541 --> 00:04:11.625
the pure energy and brilliance of this form

54
00:04:11.625 --> 00:04:15.291
makes it difficult to fully grasp.

55
00:04:15.291 --> 00:04:18.208
As Arjun reflects on this,

56
00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:23.333
he begins to understand the
truth about Lord Krishna.

57
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:24.916
He declares

58
00:04:24.916 --> 00:04:26.166
that Lord Krishna is not merely

59
00:04:26.166 --> 00:04:28.333
a great being,

60
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:30.916
but is the supreme truth itself.

61
00:04:30.916 --> 00:04:35.666
The eternal, indestructible foundation

62
00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:38.333
He recognises Lord Krishna as the shelter

63
00:04:38.333 --> 00:04:41.291
of all, the protector of eternal dharma,

64
00:04:41.291 --> 00:04:44.458
and the most ancient, eternal Person.

65
00:04:44.458 --> 00:04:45.291
This moment

66
00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:46.375
marks a transformation

67
00:04:46.375 --> 00:04:49.125
in Arjun's understanding.

68
00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:51.416
Until now, he had accepted Lord Krishna's

69
00:04:51.416 --> 00:04:53.541
wisdom and teachings,

70
00:04:53.541 --> 00:04:55.375
but now he directly

71
00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:58.083
sees the vastness of His power.

72
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:00.750
This realisation is overwhelming.

73
00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.916
It is also humbling.

74
00:05:03.916 --> 00:05:06.291
Arjun now knows that the friend

75
00:05:06.291 --> 00:05:07.791
he was speaking with

76
00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:12.000
is in truth the eternal

77
00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.750
and supreme reality behind everything.

78
00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.791
Arjun is completely absorbed

79
00:05:16.791 --> 00:05:18.833
in this divine revelation.

80
00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:21.541
He is trying to comprehend the unimaginable

81
00:05:21.541 --> 00:05:25.708
vastness of Lord Krishna's Vishwarupa.

82
00:05:30.291 --> 00:05:32.416
Think about this,

83
00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:35.500
whenever in society or in family

84
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:39.875
an important decision must be made,

85
00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:44.875
whose opinion carries the most weight?

86
00:05:44.875 --> 00:05:49.166
People begin offering opinions
even without being asked,

87
00:05:49.166 --> 00:05:51.250
but the opinion that is valued

88
00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.333
is the one behind which

89
00:05:53.333 --> 00:05:56.458
there is a foundation of
knowledge and experience.

90
00:05:56.458 --> 00:06:01.083
Suppose you want to go abroad to study.

91
00:06:01.083 --> 00:06:05.250
Then those people will guide you best

92
00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.500
who have themselves lived and studied there.

93
00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.291
Arjun

94
00:06:10.291 --> 00:06:13.416
spoke about My Vishwarupa

95
00:06:13.416 --> 00:06:15.833
only then,

96
00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:20.541
when he had seen it with divine sight.

97
00:06:20.541 --> 00:06:24.750
His words carried the weight of conviction,

98
00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:29.333
because they came from direct experience,

99
00:06:29.333 --> 00:06:33.000
not from assumption or hearsay.

100
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.208
Today, many people

101
00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:37.666
share their views on God,

102
00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:40.500
spirituality, and life,

103
00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.291
without truly understanding the subject.

104
00:06:45.291 --> 00:06:48.208
An opinion without experience

105
00:06:48.208 --> 00:06:49.708
is like guessing the taste

106
00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:54.291
of a fruit without ever tasting it.

107
00:06:54.291 --> 00:06:56.500
True wisdom comes

108
00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:00.208
when you seek knowledge,

109
00:07:00.208 --> 00:07:02.000
reflect on it,

110
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.166
and in your own life experience its truth.

111
00:07:07.166 --> 00:07:11.958
When you speak from this height,

112
00:07:11.958 --> 00:07:16.375
then your words carry power,

113
00:07:16.375 --> 00:07:20.958
and others draw inspiration from them.

114
00:07:20.958 --> 00:07:25.208
In the same way, when you receive opinions,

115
00:07:25.208 --> 00:07:27.958
consider the source.

116
00:07:27.958 --> 00:07:30.750
Listen to those who speak from experience

117
00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.916
and understanding.

118
00:07:33.916 --> 00:07:37.125
Do not be swayed by loud,

119
00:07:37.125 --> 00:07:40.041
baseless, nonsensical claims

120
00:07:40.041 --> 00:07:44.583
shouted at the top of the voice,
and always keep this in mind.

121
00:07:44.583 --> 00:07:47.458
When you share your thoughts,

122
00:07:47.458 --> 00:07:50.166
speak with humility,

123
00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:54.958
knowing that true credibility

124
00:07:54.958 --> 00:07:56.791
comes from genuine knowledge

125
00:07:56.791 --> 00:07:59.458
and direct experience.

126
00:08:04.291 --> 00:08:06.666
In family life,

127
00:08:06.666 --> 00:08:09.750
everyone has the right to share their thoughts

128
00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.625
and opinions.

129
00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.208
But when it

130
00:08:14.208 --> 00:08:17.750
comes to making important decisions,

131
00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.541
the opinion of those with more experience

132
00:08:20.541 --> 00:08:24.375
and wisdom should be given greater weight.

133
00:08:24.375 --> 00:08:26.250
Just as,

134
00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.875
after seeing My Vishwarupa,

135
00:08:29.875 --> 00:08:33.541
because it came from direct experience,

136
00:08:33.541 --> 00:08:37.250
Arjun's words were respected,

137
00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.916
in the same way, the elders in the family,

138
00:08:40.916 --> 00:08:44.458
who have faced life's challenges

139
00:08:44.458 --> 00:08:46.625
and learned from them,

140
00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:49.750
provide such insight

141
00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.500
as is rooted in reality.

142
00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.500
This experience helps them see

143
00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.708
beyond the present,

144
00:08:58.708 --> 00:08:59.833
and guides the family

145
00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:03.833
to make such decisions

146
00:09:03.833 --> 00:09:07.916
as bring lasting peace and success.

147
00:09:07.916 --> 00:09:10.166
Buying a new home,

148
00:09:10.166 --> 00:09:13.375
arranging the marriage of children,

149
00:09:13.375 --> 00:09:16.750
choosing a hospital for the
treatment of an illness –

150
00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.166
hundreds of such decisions

151
00:09:20.166 --> 00:09:24.916
a family needs to make, ever more.

152
00:09:24.916 --> 00:09:28.000
The experience of solving every such problem

153
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.583
the elders possess.

154
00:09:30.583 --> 00:09:33.375
In the same way, modern devices –

155
00:09:33.375 --> 00:09:37.500
mobiles, computers, the internet, and so on –

156
00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:42.000
the experience of these the youth have better.

157
00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.333
Drawing on everyone's experience in the family,

158
00:09:45.333 --> 00:09:48.458
a solution should be found.

159
00:09:48.458 --> 00:09:53.041
Respecting experience brings resolution.

160
00:09:53.041 --> 00:09:57.458
This advice is not based on assumption.

161
00:09:57.458 --> 00:10:02.083
It comes from understanding
relationships, overcoming obstacles,

162
00:10:02.083 --> 00:10:05.666
and observing the long-term effects

163
00:10:05.666 --> 00:10:08.125
of choices over years.

164
00:10:08.125 --> 00:10:10.166
The perspective of everyone in the family,

165
00:10:10.166 --> 00:10:13.708
young and old, matters.

166
00:10:13.708 --> 00:10:17.875
But when the final decision must be made,

167
00:10:17.875 --> 00:10:21.291
honouring the wisdom of those

168
00:10:21.291 --> 00:10:25.583
who have walked this path before you

169
00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:29.208
brings peace, goodwill,

170
00:10:29.208 --> 00:10:31.125
and stability to the family.

171
00:10:35.958 --> 00:10:41.333
In your professional life,
sharing your opinion is important,

172
00:10:41.333 --> 00:10:44.250
but it must be supported by clear reasoning

173
00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:47.750
and understanding.

174
00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.750
Just as Arjun described the Vishwarupa

175
00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:55.416
only after seeing it with divine sight,

176
00:10:55.416 --> 00:10:58.250
your opinion carries more weight when 

177
00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:04.583
it is supported by facts, logic, and experience.

178
00:11:04.583 --> 00:11:07.375
It is not enough to state

179
00:11:07.375 --> 00:11:09.750
what you think.

180
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.208
Also explain

181
00:11:12.208 --> 00:11:15.750
why you think it.

182
00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.541
This approach earns respect

183
00:11:19.541 --> 00:11:22.625
and also builds an atmosphere of trust.

184
00:11:22.625 --> 00:11:26.000
At the same time, remember this –

185
00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.833
that to learn valuable lessons,

186
00:11:29.833 --> 00:11:31.375
you do not need to directly

187
00:11:31.375 --> 00:11:34.291
experience everything.

188
00:11:34.291 --> 00:11:37.250
Just as, without seeing it yourself,

189
00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.666
you can benefit from Arjun's description

190
00:11:39.666 --> 00:11:43.125
of My Vishwarupa, in the same way

191
00:11:43.125 --> 00:11:47.416
you can learn from the experiences of others.

192
00:11:47.416 --> 00:11:49.958
Listen to mentors, colleagues,

193
00:11:49.958 --> 00:11:52.791
and the seniors of your industry

194
00:11:52.791 --> 00:11:55.958
who have faced challenges

195
00:11:55.958 --> 00:11:58.291
and found solutions.

196
00:11:58.291 --> 00:12:02.125
Their insight can help you avoid mistakes

197
00:12:02.125 --> 00:12:05.958
and make better decisions.

198
00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:08.541
Balancing your own reasoning

199
00:12:08.541 --> 00:12:12.500
with the lessons learned from others

200
00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:18.375
helps you grow faster, choose better options.

201
00:12:18.375 --> 00:12:19.708
It enables you

202
00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:21.083
to contribute more

203
00:12:21.083 --> 00:12:25.500
effectively in your organisation.
